# What does NOT travel inside the editor.
#
# The source is compiled to `out/` by `build/build-connector.sh` before packing, and the editor
# only ever loads `out/extension.js`. Shipping the TypeScript as well would put a copy of the
# source inside every installation for no reader, and would let a stale `.ts` disagree with
# the `.js` the editor actually runs.
src/**
tsconfig.json
**/*.ts
**/*.map
node_modules/**

# Half-done translations (`node build/l10n.mjs split` writes them there, including under
# `l10n/`): they are not the user's to receive. The pattern needs the leading `**/` — without it a
# `.work/**` only matches a `.work` sitting at the extension's root.
**/.work/**
.work/**
